3,0],[3,3,3,3,3,3,3,0,3,3,3,3,3,2,3,3,3,3,3,0],[2,2,2,2,2,3,3,0,3,3,3,3,3,2,3,3,3,3,3,0],[3,3,3,3,3,3,3,0,3,3,3,3,3,2,3,3,3,3,3,0],[3,3,3,3,3,3,3,0,3,3,3,3,3,2,3,3,3,3,3,0],[0,0,0,0,3,3,3,0,3,3,3,3,3,2,3,3,3,3,3,0],[0,0,0,0,3,3,3,0,3,3,3,3,3,2,3,3,3,3,3,0],[0,0,0,0,3,3,3,0,3,3,3,3,3,2,3,3,3,3,3,0],[0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,3,3,3,3,3,2,3,3,3,3,3,0],[0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,3,3,3,3,3,2,3,3,3,3,3,0],[0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,3,3,3,3,3,2,3,3,3,3,3,0],[0,0,0,0,0,0,0,3,3,3,3,3,3,2,3,3,3,3,3,3],[0,0,0,0,0,0,0,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3],[0,0,0,0,0,0,0,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3],[0,0,0,0,0,0,0,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3],[0,0,0,0,0,0,0,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3],[0,0,0,0,0,0,0,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3]]}]},"teaching_variant":"canonical","teacher_models":["claude-opus-5-5"],"explanation":"## How I read the puzzle\n\n**What the grid contains.** Every input has a background of 0 and exactly two solid rectangles of colour 3. Each rectangle has one cell of colour 2 sitting on its border. Nothing else is present.\n\n**What changes.** In each output, a \"road\" grows out of each rectangle from its 2-cell:\n- A line of 2 starts next to the marker and runs perpendicular to the edge the marker sits on, outward, all the way to the grid border.\n- The line is flanked by 3s, forming a strip parallel to it.\n\nExamples:\n- Pair 1, first rectangle (rows 3–5, cols 0–13): the 2 is at (3,5) on the top edge. Column 5 becomes 2 for rows 0–2, and columns 3–7 around it become 3.\n- Pair 1, second rectangle: the marker is at (14,10) on the left edge. Row 14 becomes 2 leftward, and rows 10–18 around it become 3.\n\n**How wide the strip is.** The half-width differs between rectangles, so I compared it with each rectangle's thickness, measured perpendicular to the marked edge:\n\n| pair | thickness | strip half-width |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 (rect 1) | 3 rows | 2 |\n| 1 (rect 2) | 5 cols | 4 |\n| 2 (rect 1) | 2 | 1 |\n| 2 (rect 2) | 3 | 2 |\n| 3 (rect 1) | 5 | 4 (clipped by the grid edge) |\n| 3 (rect 2) | 4 | 3 |\n| 4 (both) | 2 | 1 |\n\nSo **half-width = thickness − 1**. The strip covers 2·thickness − 1 cells across, centred on the 2-line, clipped to the grid.\n\n**Which edge.** The marker always lies on exactly one side of its rectangle and is not on a corner. That side decides the direction:\n\n| marker on | road extends |\n|---|---|\n| top row | up |\n| bottom row | down |\n| left column | left |\n| right column | right |\n\nAs a safety rule I only paint over background cells. In no pair does a strip cross the other rectangle, so this choice is never actually exercised.\n\n## Applying it to the test\n\n- **Rectangle at cols 4–6, rows 0–10.** The marker (5,4) is on the left edge and the thickness is 3. Row 5 at cols 0–3 becomes 2. Rows 3–7 at cols 0–3 become 3.\n- **Rectangle at rows 14–19, cols 7–19.** The marker (14,13) is on the top edge and the thickness is 6. Column 13 at rows 0–13 becomes 2. Columns 8–18 at rows 0–13 become 3. This strip stays clear of the first rectangle, which occupies cols 4–6.\n\nThe program emits one canvas after each rectangle's road is drawn, then emits the final grid.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    bg = background(g)\n    out = g.copy()\n    H, W = g.shape\n    comps = components(g != bg)\n    for cells in comps:\n        twos = [(y, x) for (y, x) in cells if g[y, x] == 2]\n        if not twos:\n            continue\n        y0, x0, y1, x1 = bbox(cells)\n        my, mx = twos[0]\n        # (dy, dx, thickness) for each edge the marker lies on, with room outward\n        opts = []\n        if my == y0 and y0 > 0:\n            opts.append((-1, 0, y1 - y0 + 1))\n        if my == y1 and y1 < H - 1:\n            opts.append((1, 0, y1 - y0 + 1))\n        if mx == x0 and x0 > 0:\n            opts.append((0, -1, x1 - x0 + 1))\n        if mx == x1 and x1 < W - 1:\n            opts.append((0, 1, x1 - x0 + 1))\n        if not opts:\n            continue\n        dy, dx, t = opts[0]\n        hw = t - 1\n        y, x = my + dy, mx + dx\n        while 0 <= y < H and 0 <= x < W:\n            for k in range(-hw, hw + 1):\n                if dy != 0:\n                    yy, xx = y, mx + k\n                else:\n                    yy, xx = my + k, x\n                if 0 <= yy < H and 0 <= xx < W and out[yy, xx] == bg:\n                    out[yy, xx] = 2 if k == 0 else 3\n            y += dy\n            x += dx\n        emit(out.copy(), f\"From the 2 marker at ({my},{mx}) draw a 2-line outward to the border, flanked by 3s for {hw} cells each side (rectangle thickness {t} minus 1).\")\n    emit(out.copy(), \"Final grid: both rectangles have their striped roads extended to the border.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"rays":[{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Final grid: both rectangles have their striped roads extended to the border."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"d896ac04da969132e2e9156bc68ecb41e3a82504021dd166d33c9702549c29b0","task_sha256":"fd9815d484a896cafbbc0b660d480660c0580df67ff1915b0c4e04ce2641a96a","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
